      "learned": "Students learned that experts — scientists, farmers, and doctors alike — routinely reach reliable conclusions about things they cannot see directly (soil chemistry, pathogens, atomic structures) by reading visible patterns and evidence. They learned that this inferential power is the foundation of science and is practiced daily in Kenya. Students also generated their first personal questions for the Driving Question Board (DQB), revealing prior knowledge gaps the teacher can use diagnostically. Pedagogical note: The DQB questions students generate here are DATA — photograph or record them. They will be revisited and refined in Lessons 7 and 8 to demonstrate cumulative learning.",
